.\" zshrs.1 — man page for zshrs(1)
.\" Companion: zshrsall(1) — comprehensive reference covering the
.\" daemon, AOT compiler, fusevm bytecode runtime, AOP intercepts,
.\" parity modes, caches, and recorder.
.TH ZSHRS 1 "2026-07-14" "zshrs 0.12.14" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zshrs \- the first compiled Unix shell (drop-in zsh replacement)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zshrs
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ argument
\&...]
.PP
.B zshrs
.B \-c
.I command
.RI [ argument
\&...]
.PP
.B zshrs
.B \-s
.RI [ argument
\&...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zshrs
is a drop-in replacement for the Z shell
.RB ( zsh (1)),
rewritten in Rust. It is the first Unix shell to compile to bytecode
and execute on a purpose-built virtual machine
.RB ( fusevm )
rather than walk an AST at run time. Source compatibility with zsh is
maintained at the lexer, parser, builtin, parameter, glob, and ZLE
layers; existing
.IR .zshrc ,
.IR .zprofile ,
zinit/oh-my-zsh plugins, and the
.B zsh-more-completions
corpus run unchanged.
.PP
Beyond compatibility,
.B zshrs
adds: a persistent worker pool that eliminates most
.BR fork (2)
overhead for builtins; aspect-oriented programming
.RB ( AOP )
intercepts on every command; rkyv-backed bytecode image caches for
scripts, plugins, and autoload functions; an optional
singleton coordinator daemon
.RB ( zshrs-daemon ,
see
.BR zd (1));
and ahead-of-time compilation
.RB ( AOT )
that bundles
.B fusevm
with bytecode into a single executable.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Special options
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the option summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the zshrs version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Full diagnostic report of shell health, cache state, daemon presence,
worker pool, and integrity scan results.
.SS Parser-pipeline dumpers
Each dumper writes to stdout and accepts
.B \-
for stdin.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-tokens " FILE"
Emit one
.IB TOKNAME \\t TOKSTR
line per lexer token.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-ast " FILE"
Parser AST in canonical S-expression form.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-wordcode " FILE"
Wordcode emitter output
.RB ( EPROG ,
.BR WORDS ,
.BR WC[i] ,
.BR STRS ).
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-zwc " ZWCFILE " [ FN ]
Inspect a compiled
.B .zwc
cache: list its function index, or, with
.IR FN ,
disassemble a single entry.
.SS VM debugging
.TP
.B \-\-disasm
Print
.B fusevm
opcodes for each compiled unit before VM execution. Does not suppress
execution.
.SS Parity modes
Each parity mode disables all caches and the daemon and matches the
named reference shell byte-for-byte; every
.B source
re-runs the file fresh, every
.B echo
re-fires.
.TP
.B \-\-zsh
Drop-in for
.BR /bin/zsh .
Entry point for compatibility tests.
.TP
.B \-\-bash
Drop-in for
.BR /bin/bash .
.TP
.B \-\-ksh
Drop-in for
.BR /bin/ksh
(ksh-93 semantics).
.TP
.B \-\-posix
Drop-in for
.BR /bin/sh
(Bourne / dash).
.TP
.B \-\-zsh\-compat
Legacy alias for
.BR \-\-zsh .
.PP
With no parity flag, zshrs runs in full mode: rkyv
.IR script_cache " + " plugin_cache " + " daemon
enabled.
.SS Standard zsh single-letter options
The following match
.BR zsh (1)
exactly. Long-option names follow each.
.TP
.B \-b
End option processing
.RB ( -- ).
.TP
.B \-c
Take the first argument as a command and execute it.
.TP
.B \-f
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-no\-rcs
(skip startup files).
.TP
.B \-i
Force interactive mode.
.TP
.B \-l
Force login shell.
.TP
.B \-s
Read commands from stdin.
.TP
.BI \-o " option"
Set
.I option
by name; see
.BR zshoptions (1).
.TP
.B \-v
.RB ( \-\-verbose )
echo each command line after history substitution.
.TP
.B \-x
.RB ( \-\-xtrace )
echo each command and its arguments as they are executed.
.PP
A complete table is printed by
.BR "zshrs \-\-help" .
The single-letter set tracks
.BR zsh (1)
literally:
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-d ,
.BR \-e ,
.BR \-g ,
.BR \-h ,
.BR \-k ,
.BR \-m ,
.BR \-n ,
.BR \-p ,
.BR \-r ,
.BR \-t ,
.BR \-u ,
.BR \-w ,
.BR \-y
and the upper-case
.BR \-H " " \-I " " \-J " " \-K " " \-L " " \-M " " \-N " " \-O " " \-P " " \-Q " " \-R " " \-S " " \-T " " \-U " " \-V " " \-W " " \-X " " \-Y " " \-Z
family.
.SH STARTUP FILES
zshrs reads the same startup files as
.BR zsh (1)
in the same order:
.IP "" 4
.I /etc/zshenv
.IP "" 4
.IB $ZDOTDIR /.zshenv
.RB ( $HOME
when
.B $ZDOTDIR
is unset)
.IP "" 4
.I /etc/zprofile
,
.IB $ZDOTDIR /.zprofile
(login)
.IP "" 4
.I /etc/zshrc
,
.IB $ZDOTDIR /.zshrc
(interactive)
.IP "" 4
.I /etc/zlogin
,
.IB $ZDOTDIR /.zlogin
(login)
.IP "" 4
.IB $ZDOTDIR /.zlogout
,
.I /etc/zlogout
(login shutdown)
.PP
.B \-\-no\-rcs
.RB ( \-f )
and the
.B PRIVILEGED
option modulate which files are sourced, identically to zsh.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
In addition to the standard zsh-recognised variables
.RB ( PATH ,
.BR FPATH ,
.BR HOME ,
.BR USER ,
.BR LOGNAME ,
.BR UID ,
.BR EUID ,
.BR SHELL ,
.BR TERM ,
.BR COLUMNS ,
.BR LINES ,
.BR ZDOTDIR ,
.BR TMPDIR ,
.BR MANPATH ,
.BR PS1 ,
.BR PROMPT ,
.BR RPROMPT ),
zshrs reads:
.TP
.B ZSHRS_CACHE
Directory for rkyv bytecode images (default
.IR $HOME/.cache/zshrs ).
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LOG
.BR tracing -style
filter for the structured log written to
.IR $HOME/.cache/zshrs/zshrs.log
.RB "(default " info ).
.TP
.B ZSHRS_LONG_CMD_PRE_THRESHOLD
Seconds before a long-running command warning fires.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/zshrs/
Cache root. Contains
.BR script_cache.rkyv ,
.BR plugin_cache.rkyv ,
.BR autoloads.rkyv ,
.BR catalog.db ,
.B daemon.sock
(when the daemon is running), and
.BR zshrs.log .
.TP
.I ~/.config/zshrs/zshrs-daemon.toml
Optional daemon configuration. See
.BR zd (1).
.TP
.I /etc/zshenv
,
.I ~/.zshenv
,
.I ~/.zprofile
,
.I ~/.zshrc
,
.I ~/.zlogin
,
.I ~/.zlogout
Standard zsh startup files (see
.BR "STARTUP FILES" ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B zshrs
exits with the status of the last command executed, or with the value
of
.B $?
at the time of an
.B exit
builtin call. Non-existent commands exit with status 127; permission
errors with 126.
